evals.prompt:
Summarize these MCP diagnostic records using only supplied evidence. Return only a JSON object with exactly these fields: connection (unverified, incomplete, or verified), completedCalls, missingResults, knownErrors, unknownErrorCalls, requestInputTokens, cachedInputTokens, qualityFindings. Use null for unavailable token counts or unavailable definitions. qualityFindings is a sorted list of codes missing_description:NAME or missing_input_schema:NAME for definition problems, or null if definitions are unavailable. Counting contract: completedCalls counts only calls with resultPresent exactly true; missingResults counts calls with resultPresent exactly false. Among completed calls only, knownErrors counts isError exactly Boolean true, and unknownErrorCalls counts any isError that is not a Boolean. Missing-result calls contribute to neither knownErrors nor unknownErrorCalls. A Boolean false status is a known non-error even if text contains ERROR. requestInputTokens and cachedInputTokens preserve their separate supplied counters; do not add them. configurationValid alone cannot verify connection: absent inspection means unverified, status incomplete means incomplete, and status complete means verified for this recorded inspection only. Do not access the network or modify files. Only use a shell command if needed to read a supplied SKILL.md.
Input:
{"calls": [{"isError": null, "resultPresent": true, "text": "ERROR is an example string"}, {"resultPresent": false}], "configurationValid": true, "inspection": null, "requestUsage": null}

